      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "Character Lock — one reference face, one image per queue.\n\n1. Load Image: use a clear front-facing face. Copy examples/input_ref.png into ComfyUI/input/ and select input_ref.png.\n2. Positive prompt: edit it for the scene. Queue once for direction A. Change the prompt and the seed, then queue again for direction B. Keep at most two directions.\n3. PuLID: weight 0.85, start_at 0.0, end_at 0.75.\n4. 6GB GPU: stay at 640×640, set FaceNet to CPU, and start ComfyUI with --lowvram.\n5. If you run out of memory: 512×512, weight 0.7, end_at 0.6.\n\nModels (see README for links):\nmodels/unet/flux1-schnell-Q4_K_S.gguf\nmodels/clip/clip_l.safetensors\nmodels/clip/t5xxl_fp8_e4m3fn.safetensors\nmodels/clip/EVA02_CLIP_L_336_psz14_s6B.pt\nmodels/vae/ae.safetensors\nmodels/pulid/pulid_flux_v0.9.1.safetensors\n\nIdentity uses PuLID for Flux and FaceNet. This graph has no ControlNet."
      ],
      "title": "How to use"
    },
